			"date": "2025-06-06T16:37:53.710Z",
			"content": "<p>Eyewitnesses (such as my late grandmother) still use the verb „abgeholt” – en: „picked-up“ – to describe Nazi arrests. This contrast highlights how routine and chilling the repression was ~90yrs ago : people vanished as easily as one might now be “picked up” for dinner.</p>",
